== Campaign and issues ==
After it was determined that the two-candidate runoff would consist of Tadić and Nikolić, the period after the first round voting converged on [[Accession of Serbia to the European Union|Serbia's accession to the European Union]], the status of [[Kosovo]] in Serbia's constitution, and various social issues.

On January 30, 2008, Tadić and Nikolić participated in a televised debate conducted by [[Radio Television of Serbia|RTS]].<ref name="Mondeb">{{cite web|url=http://mondo.rs/a87251/Info/Specijali/Izbori-2008/TV-duel-Tadic-i-Nikolic-obecali-bolji-zivot.html|title=Mondo: ''TV duel: Tadić i Nikolić obećali bolji život''|language=sr|date=January 30, 2008|access-date=July 5, 2017}}</ref> Tadić emphasized Serbia's accession process to the European Union, whereas Nikolić stated that Serbia needed to cooperate with both the EU and [[Russia]].<ref name="Mondeb"/> Tadić and Nikolić exchanged accusations on each of their own stances regarding the European Union. Tadić criticized Nikolić's [[Serbian Radical Party]] for its [[euroskepticism|eurosceptic]] history, after which Nikolić said that "Serbia will never be a Russian governorate, but also never a European colony."<ref name="Mondeb"/> They both shared similar concerns for corruption, poverty, and both candidates told the audience that Kosovo is an integral part of Serbia.<ref name="Mondeb"/> However, Nikolić stated in the debate that Kosovo "will declare independence as soon as the presidential election is finished."<ref name="Mondeb"/> Just over a month later, [[2008 Kosovo declaration of independence|Kosovo unilaterally declared independence from Serbia]].

